{
  "id": "fair-value-gaps",
  "order": 4,
  "course": "ict-mentorship-2016",
  "lessons": [
    "ict-33",
    "ict-35"
  ],
  "title": "Fair value gaps",
  "subtitle": "Imbalances that price comes back to fill",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "layout": "title",
      "say": "When price moves so fast that only one side gets filled, it leaves a gap. ICT calls it a fair value gap, and price often comes back to fill it."
    },
    {
      "title": "Three candles",
      "say": "Look at three candles in a row during a fast drop. The middle candle is the big one. Now compare the low of the candle on the left with the high of the candle on the right.",
      "els": [
        {
          "type": "candles",
          "stagger": 0.5,
          "ohlc": [
            [
              66,
              67,
              63,
              64
            ],
            [
              64,
              65,
              60,
              61
            ],
            [
              61,
              62,
              57,
              58
            ],
            [
              58,
              58.5,
              42,
              43
            ],
            [
              43,
              46,
              40,
              41
            ],
            [
              41,
              43,
              37,
              38
            ],
            [
              38,
              40,
              35,
              39
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "focus",
          "at": 4,
          "x1": 2,
          "x2": 4,
          "label": "Three candles",
          "color": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "marker",
          "at": 8,
          "x": 2,
          "y": 57,
          "label": "Left candle low",
          "color": "liq",
          "dx": -90
        },
        {
          "type": "marker",
          "at": 10,
          "x": 4,
          "y": 46,
          "label": "Right candle high",
          "color": "liq",
          "dx": 110
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The gap",
      "carry": "chart",
      "say": "The space between them was only offered to sellers. Buyers never got a chance to trade there. That imbalance is the fair value gap, and the market tends to return to rebalance it.",
      "els": [
        {
          "type": "zone",
          "at": 0.5,
          "y1": 46,
          "y2": 57,
          "x1": 2,
          "x2": 16,
          "label": "Fair value gap",
          "color": "accent"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The fill",
      "carry": true,
      "say": "Here price rallies back up, fills the gap, and runs out of steam. That's a short entry with a stop above the gap, aiming for the sell stops below the lows. Bullish gaps work the same way, upside down.",
      "els": [
        {
          "type": "candles",
          "at": 0.5,
          "stagger": 0.45,
          "walk": [
            [
              7,
              40
            ],
            [
              9,
              37
            ],
            [
              11,
              45
            ],
            [
              13,
              52
            ],
            [
              14,
              55
            ],
            [
              16,
              47
            ],
            [
              19,
              31
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "marker",
          "at": 3.8,
          "x": 14,
          "y": 56,
          "label": "Gap filled: sell",
          "color": "bear"
        },
        {
          "type": "level",
          "at": 5,
          "y": 58.5,
          "x1": 12,
          "x2": 17,
          "label": "Stop",
          "color": "bear"
        },
        {
          "type": "arrow",
          "at": 6.5,
          "from": [
            14.5,
            53
          ],
          "to": [
            19,
            33
          ],
          "label": "Run to the lows",
          "color": "bear"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Liquidity voids",
      "say": "Zoom out and you'll often see a liquidity void: several candles moving one way with almost no pullbacks. On lower timeframes, a daily gap usually looks like this. Expect price to return into it.",
      "points": [
        "A void is a big one-sided move over several candles",
        "Lower timeframes show daily gaps as voids",
        "Price tends to come back and fill them"
      ],
      "els": [
        {
          "type": "candles",
          "stagger": 0.25,
          "walk": [
            [
              0,
              20
            ],
            [
              2,
              23
            ],
            [
              6,
              76
            ],
            [
              8,
              72
            ],
            [
              10,
              66
            ],
            [
              11,
              60
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "zone",
          "at": 3.5,
          "y1": 26,
          "y2": 70,
          "x1": 3,
          "x2": 13,
          "label": "Liquidity void",
          "color": "accent"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Using gaps",
      "say": "Putting it together: find displacement, mark the gap from the left candle's wick to the right candle's wick, wait for price to return, and target liquidity on the other side.",
      "els": [
        {
          "type": "flow",
          "at": 0.6,
          "stagger": 2.4,
          "items": [
            {
              "label": "Find displacement",
              "sub": "A fast, one-sided move"
            },
            {
              "label": "Mark the gap",
              "sub": "Left candle's wick to right candle's wick"
            },
            {
              "label": "Wait for the return",
              "sub": "Enter as price fills it",
              "color": "liq"
            },
            {
              "label": "Target liquidity",
              "sub": "Old highs or lows beyond",
              "color": "bull"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Recap",
      "say": "Remember: markets seek efficiency. A gap where only one side traded is an imbalance, and price is often drawn back to rebalance it.",
      "els": [
        {
          "type": "big",
          "at": 0.3,
          "text": "Imbalance gets rebalanced",
          "sub": "A fair value gap is where only one side traded. Price often returns to fill it, offering an entry.",
          "color": "accent"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
